XCopy Standalone:

  Todo+ format: ☐ open, ✔ done, ✘ cancelled. An indented line with no marker is a
  note on the task above it.

  Reviewed 26-09-04 against the tree at v737.26. The list had not been touched
  since v713 and around eighty commits landed under it in the meantime, so items
  the code showed as already built were closed, and items whose premise no longer
  holds were cancelled with the reason. Both are listed together below the rule.
  Closures from that pass carry a date with no time, which is what tells them
  apart from the ones stamped by hand as the work happened.

  Everything above the rule is open, and was re-worded against the code so that
  each line says what is actually wrong and where.

Firmware:

  Drive & Disk:
    ☐ A retry count of 0 fails every read and write outright
      readDiskTrack() is `while (readResult == -1 && retries < retryCount)`, so a
      count of 0 never enters the loop, never attempts the read, and returns the
      -1 it was initialised with. writeDiskTrack() has the same shape, and the
      settings menu allows 0. XCopyDisk.cpp:304, XCopyDisk.cpp:355.
    ☐ Gather the drive timings into one struct, and persist them
      stepPulseUs, stepIntervalUs, dirSettleUs, sideSettleUs, seekSettleUs and
      motorSpinupMs are six file scope globals with a setter each, and XCopyConfig
      carries none of them - a drive tuned by hand is retuned on every boot.
      XCopyFloppy.cpp:143.
    ☐ Implement the disk delay setting
      getDiskDelay() is read in exactly two places and both are the menu line that
      displays it. Nothing in the copy path waits on it. XCopy.cpp:252, :1549.
    ☐ Verify what writebin wrote
      writeFileToBlocks() writes each track and reports the retries it took, but
      never reads a track back to compare it against the file. XCopyDisk.cpp:1736.
    ☐ Say head rather than side outside the logical track numbering
      XCopyGeometry.h settled cylinder against logical track. The other half of
      the rename did not happen: DiskLocation::side(), drawTrack() and
      sideSettleUs all still say side for what the drive calls a head.

  Console:
    ☐ One command line implementation for both processors
      ESPCommandLine::doCommand() and XCopyCommand are still two hand written
      parsers for the same job. The Teensy side gained a command table, an
      interpreter, tab completion and history at v728.26 and the ESP side did
      not. src/esp8266/ESPCommand.cpp:8.
    ☐ cd and pwd for mounted volumes
      mount, dir, cat, cp, rm and mkdir all take a whole path (dir ADF0:c), so
      there is nowhere to stand and nothing for cd to change. Only worth building
      if the typing turns out to be annoying in use.

  Web UI:
    ☐ Delete files from the browser's file browser
      rm landed on the console at v732.26. sdcard.js has no delete at all.
    ☐ Show the signal strength of the network actually joined
      RSSI is read for the scan command and thrown away everywhere else.
      ESPCommand.cpp:242.
    ☐ Tell the Web UI that the cancel wire is present
      detectCancelPin() runs at startup and its result goes to the log and nowhere
      else, so the browser cannot know whether to offer the button.
      XCopy.cpp:151, XCopy.cpp:532.
    ☐ Test for a disk before sending a block to the disk monitor
      sendBlock() seeks and reads with no diskChange() check, so an empty drive
      reads as a failed track rather than a No Disk Inserted message.
      XCopy.cpp:874.
    ☐ Disk monitor: view a mounted ADF, not only the drive
      Mounting made an image readable through the same code as the drive at
      v730.26, so there is a second source to point the viewer at now.
    ☐ Disk monitor: edit a sector and write it back
      One sector means reading the whole track, replacing 512 bytes of it and
      writing all eleven back. That is why XCopyAdfFloppyDriver is read only, and
      it is the same piece of work.
    ☐ Keep the Sass sources out of the LittleFS image
      data/css holds eleven .scss files that are only inputs to default.css.
      LittleFS rounds every file up to an 8KB block and the partition is already
      sized around a 730KB directory. platformio.ini:120.
    ☐ Send the flux samples as binary
      The ~10sec a disk test spends on flux notification was mostly the link, and
      that went to 1 Mbaud. What is left is one decimal string per sample.
    ☐ Copy files to the SPI flash from the browser
      Upload lands on the SD card and verifies itself. The flash has no path in
      from the web UI at all.
    ☐ Host the Giants manual and link it from the Web UI

  ESP & Wireless:
    ☐ Update the SSID and Password menu items when connect is used
      cmdConnect() writes the config but never touches ssidMenuItem->text or
      passwordMenuItem->text, so the settings menu shows the old network until the
      next boot. XCopyCommand.cpp:1842, XCopy.cpp:258.
    ☐ Delete and recreate _config properly at startup
      delete _config sits commented out in ten places, left that way while testing
      because the pointer is shared with XCopyCommand. Delete it at startup and
      recreate it in the connect command. XCopy.cpp:266, and nine more.

  Memory & Flash:
    ☐ Enclose the remaining strings in F()
      227 are done. What is left is mostly String concatenation in the web
      broadcast paths, which F() cannot help with on its own.
    ☐ Decide whether .begin() is still worth removing
      Twenty classes take this shape now against the handful that did in 19, and
      it is the Arduino idiom. Worth settling the question before starting. The
      other half of the original line - change local variables to pointers - is
      the opposite of what the scratch arena does, so it is not carried over.

Unverified - reported in 19, against code rewritten since:
  Each of these needs a re-test on hardware before it is worth acting on. If one
  no longer reproduces, cancel it; if it does, it needs a repro written down.

  ☐ Audio fires more than once when scrolled past a screenful of entries
  ☐ Crash entering a sub directory with files, backing out, entering an empty one,
    moving up and down, and backing out again
    The listing has been rewritten twice since this was seen (b82393d, cbb7822)
    and again at v726.26, and the sibling crash next to it was fixed in 19.
  ☐ SerialFlash create / createErasable, and why the config write works
    Two lines said this twice - SdFat seems to have broken SerialFlash create /
    createErasable, and have a look at configfile write and createerasable, why
    does it currently work. writeConfig() still removes the file and creates it
    again, which the 19 archive claims was replaced by an overwrite.
    XCopyConfig.cpp:180.
  ☐ diskname returns NDOS for a DOS disk until the drive is reset
  ☐ The download occasionally resends the file
    Suspected to be Content-Length at the time. The ESP now calls
    setContentLength(filesize) before streaming and the transfer has an idle
    timeout, so this may already be gone. esp8266.cpp:180.
  ☐ ADFlib sometimes crashes on NDOS disks - try workbnch then mutation
  ☐ Sound is lost after rawDraw, root cause never found
    The temporary fix that suppressed drawing while audio played is no longer in
    XCopyGraphics, so this either went away or is live and unguarded.

