Closed by the 26-09-04 review:
  Open items the code showed as built, or whose premise no longer holds. The
  version in brackets is where the work landed.

  Built since v713:
    ✔ Run the xterm console over the websocket directly @done(26-09-04)
      term.write() is driven from websocket.js, and the connection layer was
      rebuilt around real socket state (247bc5e).
    ✔ File upload not reliable - sometimes too short @done(26-09-04)
      Per chunk ACK in place of open loop pacing, and a 4096 byte Serial1 RX ring
      (2d46027).
    ✔ Add uploaded filesize does not match saved filesize error @done(26-09-04)
      CRC32 and byte count receipt; upload.js verifies ok/size/crc32 rather than
      treating any 200 as success (2d46027).
    ✔ Speed up file transfer @done(26-09-04)
      The ESP link went from 115200 to 1 Mbaud (2d46027, XCopyProtocol.h:51).
    ✔ Increase serial baud rate @done(26-09-04)
      Same change. Was listed twice, under file transfer and under diskflux.
    ✔ Migrate XCopyDisk to XCopyFloppy routines @done(26-09-04)
      The driver became a class (4f2730a); XCopyDisk has no hardware access left
      and every MFM routine lives in XCopyFloppy.
    ✔ Add cursor to logging console @done(26-09-04)
      XCopyLineEditor: cursor, CSI sequences, history and tab completion (v728.26).
    ✔ Increase ping time out @done(26-09-04)
      Superseded - liveness is stamped from any inbound frame and pings are
      suppressed entirely while the device is busy (247bc5e).
    ✔ Fix time commands @done(26-09-04)
      time, timezone and settime came through the table driven rewrite (v728.26).
    ✔ Implement and test manual set time and get time from PC @done(26-09-04)
      settime --epoch <n> (XCopyCommandTable.cpp:127).
    ✔ Fix command line so it doesn't repeat a command for CR+LF @done(26-09-04)
      Both editors submit on 0x0d or 0x0a and an empty line returns early
      (XCopyLineEditor.cpp:119, XCopyCommand.cpp:208, ESPCommand.cpp:406).
    ✔ Add paging of large directories @done(26-09-04)
      The listing is a window onto the list and scrolls under the cursor
      (XCopyDirectory.h:82); MAXSCREENITEMS no longer exists.
    ✔ Add support for floppy drive in myinit, myread etc @done(26-09-04)
      XCopyAdfFloppyDriver - the disk in the drive as an ADFlib device (v731.26).
    ✔ Implement myFunctions @done(26-09-04)
      ADFlib 0.10.7 with real drivers instead of edits to the library (v729.26).
    ✔ Add support for mount, dir, cd @done(26-09-04)
      mount, unmount, dir, cat, cp, rm and mkdir over images and DF0: (v730.26,
      v731.26, v732.26). cd was the one piece not built and is re-raised above.
    ✔ Copy files to the SD card from the PC @done(26-09-04)
      Browser upload, verified end to end. The flash half is re-raised above.
    ✔ Add ESP reset (pin 25) and program (gpio0, pin 26) @done(26-09-04)
      PIN_ESPRESETPIN and PIN_ESPPROGPIN are driven for programming mode, and OTA
      arrived on top of it (XCopyPins.h:14).
    ✔ Move the modified SDFat library into local library @done(26-09-04)
      lib/SdFat.
    ✔ Report weak tracks in diskcopy, test and flux @done(26-09-04)
      readDiskTrack() marks a weak track yellow on the TFT, the console map and
      the web grid, and the ADF log records a per track count (XCopyDisk.cpp:314).
    ✔ Add remaining serial commands @done(26-09-04)
      49 commands in a table with help and completion (v728.26).
    ✔ Hookup SD card detect @done(26-09-04)
      PIN_CARDDETECT is wired and read, and drives the insert and eject audio.
      The v3 footprint fix is a separate item and is still open.

  Premise no longer holds:
    ✘ Reduce the stream object from streamSizeHD to streamSizeDD (13k) @cancelled(26-09-04)
      Written while HD support is removed. It is not: densityDetect() and
      hdDisk() are live and readTrack() uses the HD sized stream.
    ✘ Delete _disk when not being used to free up memory @cancelled(26-09-04)
      _disk is a member object, not a heap pointer, and the scratch arena is how
      big transient buffers are found now (XCopyScratch).
    ✘ Only create ADFx when needed @cancelled(26-09-04)
      The ADFx classes were renamed XCopyX in 19. Mount slots replaced the idea.
    ✘ Rewrite track read, track write and MFM encode / decode @cancelled(26-09-04)
      Rewrite to what end was never stated, so nothing could ever finish it. The
      routines were moved into a class and hardened since - bounds checked decode,
      bounded index waits, a corrected decode clock. Raise something specific if
      there is still a problem with them.
    ✘ Move graphics calls into classes and have all items called update @cancelled(26-09-04)
      Too vague to act on and no longer describes the code.
    ✘ Investigate bugs with multiple << and printf @cancelled(26-09-04)
      No repro was recorded and the console has been rebuilt since.
    ✘ Test different S7735 libraries to see if faster @cancelled(26-09-04)
      The redraw cost this was chasing was fixed differently: two changed rows are
      repainted instead of the whole screen (v726.26).

